RUN_REVIEW_FULL #+TITLE: Ora procurement run review
#+DATE: 2026-10-07
#+AUTHOR: Omega

* Instruction compliance
- Read instructions.bl.org: yes.
- Used real task-owned browser through browser-tool.mjs: yes.
- Wrote all four deliverables: company.bl.org, search.bl.org, opportunities.bl.org, run-review.bl.org: yes.
- No applications, registration, messages or payments: yes. No form submissions beyond public search forms; no login/registration.
- No spawning other tasks: yes.
- Bounded source reads: roughly 12 browser source loads; stopped TED after WAF and did not repeat capability pages.
- Original-notice separation: verified Morocco detail URLs came from PMMP result rows; France detail URLs came from PLACE result rows. EU-wide remains unverified/blocked.

* Generated-function execution proof
- Named defns defined in Omega eval and persisted in search.bl / search.bl.org: bt-arg, bt-noarg, bt-eval, bt-links, bt-open, page-text, page-url, capture-evidence, ma-keyword, ma-rows, fr-place-open, fr-place-text, fr-place-search, fr-place-links, ted-open, ted-search, ted-text, ted-links.
- Executed ma-keyword "intelligence artificielle" → PMMP result list included 16/BNRM/2026 and DA/15/26; ma-rows produced their detail URLs.
- Executed fr-place-search "intelligence artificielle" → PLACE result list included 2025-0154-00-00-MPF and EC071026; link inspection produced detail URLs.
- Executed ted-search "artificial intelligence" → TED landing did not apply query and later WAF/human verification blocked advanced search and API.
- Evidence files: evidence-morocco-ia.txt, evidence-france-ia-v3.txt.

* Failed tools/sources
- `js/JSON.parse` unavailable in BEAM Lisp; functions therefore return sh/plain text instead of parsing JSON.
- Initial bt-arg shell single-quote transport broke JS expressions containing single quotes (selectors, Event('change'), 'submitted'). Repaired with v3 using the supplied `--arg-file` verbatim transport.
- `java.net.URLEncoder` was unavailable on BEAM; replaced with `str/replace` for simple space-to-%20 in TED query.
- TED search: direct query ignored by landing page; advanced search and API returned AWS WAF human verification or method-not-supported. No alternate EU-wide official source completed in the remaining budget.
- PLACE row-href extraction with a `tr` selector returned `[]`; a broader `a` selector found detail links.

* Unresolved discrepancies
- PMMP page URL immediately after form submission sometimes still showed the advanced-search URL while body text showed result rows; treated body text plus captured evidence URL as authoritative.
- Time zones: PMMP and PLACE displayed deadlines without explicit timezone. Morocco was read as local Morocco time; France presumed CET/CEST but not independently labeled.
- Ora's domicile/registration/languages/references/certifications were not present on the homepage; left as unknowns, not inferred.
- The Morocco GPU notice is a rental/infrastructure tender and the ONMT notice is Qlik-specific; neither directly proves Ora's ability to deliver those scopes.
- TED country restriction in an earlier draft (`buyer-country=FRA&buyer-country=MAR`) was removed in final function/source block for EU coverage, but no EU-wide result was obtained.

* User-experience friction
- PMMP is form-state heavy (PRADO_PAGESTATE) and refs change; quick search was less useful than advanced keyword.
- PLACE is easier for public search but detail links only surfaced through anchor inspection.
- TED WAF was the largest friction; browser automation was halted before useful search results.
- `subs` errors when slicing a short string consumed one eval step; later avoided slicing.

* Final files
- company.bl.org, search.bl.org, search.bl, opportunities.bl.org, run-review.bl.org
- evidence-morocco-ia.txt, evidence-france-ia-v3.txt

BROWSER_TOOL_HEAD import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
// Infrastructure only; the model authors its own curated functions around this.
const [action,...args]=process.argv.slice(2);
try {
  if(args[0]==='--arg-file'){
    if(args.length!==2)throw Error('Use ACTION --arg-file PATH for one literal argument.');
    const argument=await fs.readFile(args[1],'utf8');args.splice(0,args.length,argument);
  }
  const task=process.env.OMEGA_TASK_TAG?.split(':').at(-1);
  if(!task)throw Error('Run this helper inside an Omega eval shell (OMEGA_TASK_TAG).');
  const briefExists=await fs.access('company.bl.org').then(()=>true,()=>false);
  if(briefExists){
    const functions=await fs.readFile('search.bl','utf8').catch(()=> '');
    const strategy=await fs.readFile('search.bl.org','utf8').catch(()=> '');
    if(!functions.includes('(defn ') || !strategy.includes('#+begin_src'))
      throw Error('Research checkpoint: company brief exists. Before further browser operations, author named curated defn functions in search.bl and matching documented source blocks in search.bl.org, then execute those functions inside Omega eval.');
  }
  let operation=action,operationArgs=args;
  if(action==='wait'){
    const ms=Number(args[0]);
    if(args.length!==1 || !Number.isInteger(ms) || ms<0 || ms>10000)throw Error('Wait duration must be 0..10000 ms');
    operation='eval';operationArgs=[`new Promise(resolve=>setTimeout(()=>resolve("page wait complete"),${ms}))`];
  }
  const response=await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8797/browser/tool',{
    method:'POST',headers:{'content-type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({task,action:operation,args:operationArgs})});
  const result=await response.json();
  if(!response.ok || !result.ok)throw Error(result.message || 'Browser operation failed');
  const value=result.result;
  // Keep browser launch diagnostics out of model context; preserve useful page data.
  let output=value?.result ?? value;
  if(typeof output==='string'){
    try {output=JSON.parse(output);}catch {}
  }
  if(output && typeof output==='object' && !Array.isArray(output)){
    output={...output};delete output.lifecycle;
  }
  if(action==='snapshot' && output?.snapshot)console.log(output.snapshot);
  else if(typeof output==='string')console.log(output);
  else console.log(JSON.stringify(output));
}catch(error){console.error(error.message);process.exitCode=1;}
